  "title": "Report of the Advisory Committee on Ways and Means Advances to State Governments",
  "summary": "The Reserve Bank of India has today placed on its website the Report of the Advisory Committee on Ways and Means Advances (WMA) to State Governments . The Reserve Bank had constituted an Advisory Committee, under the Chairmanship of Shri I S N Prasad, former Additional Chief Secretary, Government of Karnataka. The terms of reference of the Advisory Committee included, inter alia, review of State-wise WMA limits and other financial accommodation facilities available to the States. The Committee has made various recommendations which shall be examined by the Reserve Bank. (Brij Raj) Chief Genera",
